 (* agent note (|2026-09-15 STORAGE SUBSTRATE WATCH (operator review
      session, PP archaeology). Pricklypear's one-tree substrate
      autopsy, tl;dr: its "everything is a tree" storage bet froze at
      HALF-migrated (P3 read-flip done, P4 write-truth never retired
      the relational tables) and that intermediate dual-run state is
      precisely where weeks of vibecoding got spent: user-owned
      mutable path hierarchies force a path grammar, a label codec,
      branch-override walks, version shadows, sibling order, retention
      policies, and generations — seven subsystems, all paid for and
      none of them load-bearing for the calculus. LESSON, to be kept
      standing law for tuna1 AND tuna2: content-addressed VALUES are
      the primitive; mutable tree HIERARCHIES in PG storage are the
      vibecoding trap. tuna1's store (0001 flat tables) is clean; keep
      it so — every new table that prefers a path or a parent pointer
      over a hash should be questioned in review. Explored nightly
      drafts for v2 (D7: canonical-hash preimage off ternary text onto
      packed bitstream, plus post-GC temporal KV, Model-B
      merkelized-node materialization on demand) live outside this
      repo at ~/dev/wyo.tech/tuna2/spec-draft-v0.md and are NOT M9/M10
      scope; the jam is documenting intent so neither the next loop
      HERE nor the next ten conversation partners relitigate the PP
      substrate on fresh foot.|) *)
 (* agent note (|2026-09-15 OPERATOR DECISION - CLUB REPURPOSE + M10
      SUBSTRATE SLICE (relayed live by gregor; supersedes the
      "v2 exploration deferred" clause of the STORAGE SUBSTRATE WATCH
      for this slice only - the values-law itself stands and binds this
      slice). roerick repurposes the pricklypear.club instance: tuna
      becomes the club runtime tonight (relayd flip to tuna; PP kept
      dark on :18080 with its data preserved in place). Shipping now on
      top of the v1 store: (1) paths are DERIVED - a path->value-hash
      index over content-addressed values; no path or parent pointer is
      ever storage truth; (2) writes are versioned CAS on value hash;
      every op lands in a sha256-chained effect log; (3) grants name
      path prefixes (garden shape); (4) prims tree/get, tree/put,
      tree/cas, tree/list, ns/fork; rewind = fold of the effect log at
      a seq; (5) the calculus sees none of it - paths arrive only as
      granted arguments (SPEC 4.4 ambient-authority ban stands).
      M9 REPL untouched. Gate before push: build, runtest,
      differential, smoke.|) *)
 (* agent note (|2026-10-02 DESIGN REVIEW SESSION with the operator
      (host-agent conversation over the roadmap, naming, and the
      monetization proposals). Outcomes recorded so neither the next
      loop nor the next operator conversation relitigates:
      (1) stdlib v1 chapter landed this session (borg/stdlib.borg,
      commit 47d43de) and carries the vocabulary-first dogfood gate:
      no in-calculus product logic until its vocabulary and
      acceptance exist, else dogfood false-negatives a bare
      language. (2) forensics chapter added (borg/forensics.borg):
      the 'extremely debuggable' pitch made falsifiable on a
      deliberate-fault corpus with frozen gates and F7; of the two
      count laws bruited in review only determinism survives - a
      constant swap preserves the count while changing behavior,
      and the chapter refuses to resurrect the stronger claim.
      (3) F5/F6 trigger numbers accepted as written, owner-retunable
      in the open. OPERATOR VOCABULARY SEAL (pin it): 'tuna is the
      Haskell to Nopales' OCaml' - effects as asked/answered/
      re-answered data surrounding a pure fold, versus ambient
      state woven through evaluation; the distinction is existing
      book law (journal chapter, runtime purity thesis) now with
      operator phrasing to hand future agents. NAMING: sabra (v0
      runner-up) is the owner's leaning for the language split
      (tuna = system, sabra = surface dialect); owner's call,
      frozen nowhere, nothing depends on it - stdlib chapter
      artifacts are name-stable either way. ECONOMICS: SPECULATIVE,
      PARKED, expressly NOT spec'd (direction only): artifact
      gating is unforceable by architecture - the hash IS the
      capability, bytes must flow to run or verify, replay identity
      inverts pay-per-use - so royalties, minting and per-use fees
      do not spec on this substrate. The enforceable seam is
      settlement only (a club may gate payouts, never execution);
      the honest value forms, IF ever wanted: metered tenancy
      priced on fuel (the substrate-native unit - every run row
      carries exact steps plus its semantics pin), an
      open-collective-shaped maintenance tithe anchored externally
      (operators, patrons, host revenue), and witness logs
      (certificate-transparency pattern) as the only honest 'proof
      of proof' - third parties publishing their exit-0 deriv-check
      records; verification itself stays free, exit-0, forever, no
      gates ever. Litmus recorded: FOLLOW THE OUTSIDE MONEY - if
      every collectable dollar traces to another member's entry
      fee, it is the same pyramid in a new hat. The one genuinely
      novel direction noted (not scheduled): sealed deriv records
      as receipts for agent work - the dogfood path someday is PP
      workstream cards sealed via the planned F3 bridge, AFTER
      forensics (which runs fully in-tree); no marketplaces, no
      tokens, and receipts get built only when a stranger asks.
      Sequencing stands: stdlib v1 -> forensics -> F3 bridge;
      product candidates (ledger first) ride the stdlib mole
      scenario acceptance. |) *)
